# Safari Tools Implementation (PHASE 2 COMPLETED ✅)

## Overview
The Juno AI Computer Use Agent now includes **specialized Safari DOM automation tools** that provide 3-5x faster Safari-specific operations through direct AppleScript/JavaScript injection. This implementation represents the completed Phase 2 of the Juno-Opus integration project.

## Architecture

### Core Module
- **[safari_tools.rs](mdc:dotdot/dotdot/src-tauri/src/agent/tools/safari_tools.rs)**: Main implementation with `SafariTools` struct
- **[safari_tools.rs](mdc:dotdot/dotdot/src-tauri/src/commands/safari_tools.rs)**: Tauri commands for agent integration
- **Tool Registration**: Integrated in [factory.rs](mdc:dotdot/dotdot/src-tauri/src/agent/providers/factory.rs) via `register_safari_tools()`
- **Agent Templates**: Full documentation in [templates.rs](mdc:dotdot/dotdot/src-tauri/src/agent/prompts/templates.rs)

### Key Components

#### SafariTools Struct
```rust
#[derive(Clone)]
pub struct SafariTools {
    element_cache: Arc<Mutex<HashMap<String, SafariElement>>>,
    performance_metrics: Arc<Mutex<SafariMetrics>>,
}
```

#### Available Tools
1. **`safari_get_url`**: Gets current Safari page URL
2. **`safari_navigate`**: Navigates Safari to specified URL
3. **`safari_click_element`**: Clicks elements by CSS selector
4. **`safari_get_text`**: Extracts text content from elements
5. **`safari_fill_form`**: Fills form fields with specified values
6. **`safari_execute_script`**: Executes custom JavaScript in Safari

